  "summary": "Collection of bundled skill scripts with routine network and install commands",
  "details": "Package bundles a collection of skill scripts under bundled-skills/. Static pattern matches fire on ordinary shell/Python constructs: a Python base scraper that performs HTTP GET/POST and uses 'ping' as an identifier/health keyword; a serve_api.py that defines GET route handlers; a run-benchmarks.sh containing an \"install\": JSON-like key and a curl invocation; an rclone install.sh that fetches rclone from https://rclone.org (the project's official domain); and a youtube-notetaker verify.sh that curls public endpoints. No hardcoded attacker-controlled destination is wired to installer-secret reads, no lifecycle (preinstall/install/postinstall) fetch-and-execute of attacker-controlled code is present, and no credential, env-var, wallet, or home-directory scanning is observed. These are routine HTTP client, documented tool installer, and benchmarking patterns rather than exfiltration or install-time RCE.",
